3. Row 11: `3 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6` → `3 6 6 6 6 6 2 6 6`: 6 at col 6 became 2 because row 12 has 3 at col 6
4. Row 12: `3 6 3 6 3 6 3 6 6` → `3 2 3 2 3 2 3 6 6`: 6s BETWEEN 3s on SAME row become 2s

The pattern: Background cells become 2 if they're in a continuous region CONNECTED to the pattern/walls (of 3s). This is "filling" the enclosed area.

